BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hutch &amp\; Friends Pride Edition
DTSTART:20260626T203000
DTEND:20260626T203000
UID:0c29e3bff77d6c00dcf7f6d5096a833e@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Host Paul Hutcheson is a queer comedic performer\, writer and 
 producer. His six solo shows have been produced numerous comedic solo show
 s which have toured Canada and the United States\, playing to sold-out aud
 iences\, glowing reviews and awards. He produces monthly comedy events Hut
 ch &amp\; Friends and Hutch’s Storytime in Toronto. His comedy album\, C
 all Me Hutch\, is produced by Howl &amp\; Roar Records. Please visit canuc
 khutch.com for more information. Performers Martha Chaves is an award-winn
 ing stand-up comedian\, actor\, writer\, and keynote speaker who has been 
 making Canada laugh for over two decades. Martha tours coast to coast. In 
 2023\, she was part of the Gala the Root of All Evil at the Winnipeg Comed
 y Festival\, which earned a Canadian Screen Award nomination. She’s a re
 gular on CBC’s Because News and Laugh Out Loud and a veteran of Just For
  Laughs\, the Winnipeg Comedy Fest and more. Based in Toronto\, Adrienne F
 ish has recorded four performances for national television\, including an 
 appearance at Montreal&#x27\;s Just For Laughs Festival as part of Canada&
 #x27\;s Homegrown Comics\, airing on CTV Comedy Channel and CraveTV. She h
 as appeared on Season 2 of CTV&#x27\;s Roast Battle Canada and is regularl
 y featured across North America on Sirius XM radio and was nominated for t
 wo Canadian Comedy Awards including Breakout Artist of the Year. Nile Segu
 in has performed at the Just for Laughs Festival\, San Francisco Sketchfes
 t\, the Winnipeg Comedy Festival\, the Halifax Comedy Festival and the Bos
 ton Comedy Festival. A three-time Canadian Comedy Award nominee\, he has a
 lso opened for James Adomian\, Janeane Garofalo and Hannibal Buress. Nile 
 has written for Comedy Network’s The Beaverton as well as This Hour Has 
 22 Minutes\, Tallboys\, the Gemini Award winning The Hour. He was also nom
 inated for a Canadian Screen Award for his writing on CBC’s Still Standi
 ng and most recently Nile his solo podcast Total Nileation. Jonathan Barri
 e is a Toronto-based storyteller and comedian who loves to share his (mis)
 adventures on stage. Trained at Second City and Comedy Bar\, he takes audi
 ences on hilarious\, heartfelt journeys. Catch him lighting up storytellin
 g shows and open mics across the GTA. Often called clever\, unique and lat
 e for dinner Jordan Trafford is a Toronto based comic with a self-deprecat
 ing style that can be best described by someone else. Most noted for his o
 ne liners and quirky word play Jordan recently realized being self-conscio
 us sounds like being self-aware and likes that. When not performing Jordan
  can most likely be found funny. @canuckhutch canuckhutch.com ‍
LOCATION:Burdock Music Hall\, 1184 Bloor St W
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/hutch-friends-pride-edition-2
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
