BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:- shoplifter + digital polyglot + QQ
DTSTART:20260710T220000
DTEND:20260710T220000
UID:4ce5e773ed7cf8e0e5c53eec1a24f400@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Venus Fest is taking over The Jama for a late-night dance part
 y on College Street. Expect a sweaty\, high-energy room soundtracked by 
 ​shoplifter (belgium) digital polyglot ​QQ Join us with your friends\,
  lovers\, and family! ​Advanced tickets are 20$ | Doors 25$ shoplifter O
 ne of the fastest-rising names in the Belgian electronic underground\, sho
 plifter has quickly established herself as a DJ with a finely tuned sense 
 of dancefloor intuition. With musical foundations rooted in UK bass\, brea
 kbeats and dub-adjacent club mu sic\, her sets unfold within an organic\, 
 free-flowing narrative\, emphasizing the warm\, wonky and immersive aspect
 s of club music. digital polyglot digital polyglot is a versatile artist w
 ith DJ sets that transcend borders and genres. They blend an array of afro
 diasporic sounds into their performances — drawn to whatever feels raw\,
  hard-hitting and transcendent. They&#x27\;ve graced both party and festiv
 al stages including Piknic Électronik\, L&#x27\;après Osheaga\, Fierté 
 Montréal\, Club Quarantine\, Pride Toronto\, POP Montréal and more. ​Q
 Q QQ is a multidisciplinary artist\, musical human\, daydreamer &amp\; pra
 ctitioner of Traditional Medicine. With roots in queer-punk DIY scenes\, a
 nd a long history of playing in garage\, punk and ambient bands\, the tran
 sition to dj was an unnatural-next-step-turned-obsession. As a taiko drumm
 er\, QQ loves the driving rhythms of techno. ‍
LOCATION:The Jama\, 961 College St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/shoplifter-digital-polyglot-qq
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:IOU presents D. Tiffany - 4AM LAST CALL
DTSTART:20260710T220000
DTEND:20260710T220000
UID:8b976cbeb81bd68b24a53f679222a86c@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:/lineup D. Tiffany Milch (1) Rabzi 99hp The enigmatic and prol
 ific D. Tiffany returns to her native land. Based in Berlin for much of th
 e last decade\, Sophie Sweetland has long been one of the underground&#x27
 \;s most inventive and forward-thinking voices. Her projects span genres a
 nd styles across the more adventurous corners of electronic music: off kil
 ter dark-tronica\, &quot\;Canadian Riviera&quot\; deep house\, pumping tra
 nce &amp\; techno\, IDM\, ambient - you name it. Beyond her productions an
 d DJ-ing\, Sweetland&#x27\;s work behind the scenes through her labels (in
 cluding Planet Euphorique\, Plush Records Inc.\, Delicate Records\, and mo
 re) has helped shape the sound and direction of contemporary dance music. 
 As a curator\, tastemaker\, and champion of emerging artists\, she has cem
 ented her place as one of the most influential figures in electronic music
 . IOU is honoured and excited to bring her back to Toronto for the first t
 ime in nearly three years for this special 4AM last call event. Providing 
 support: IOU executives Rabzi &amp\; 99hp\, plus Cafeteria queen Milch. 
 ‍
LOCATION:Cafeteria\, 1650 Dupont Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/iou-presents-d-tiffany---4am-last-call
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
